WEBVTT

00:00:30.823 --> 00:00:32.449
I won't let you pass.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:35.286
Shana, didn't I tell you before?

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:39.832
That I will never stand with you,
as long as you're a Flame Haze.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.295
Because the Flame Hazes will never
be able to forgive the Denizens.

00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:49.091
They reject them as something
that is foreign to this world!

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.012
Therefore, I shall create
the paradise Xanadu,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.472
and take the Denizens from this world.

00:00:55.681 --> 00:01:00.227
And for the first time, they'll live in a
world they want, one that wants them.

00:01:00.436 --> 00:01:02.813
They will truly belong.

00:01:03.022 --> 00:01:08.068
At the same time, this is the one
way to grant Yuji Sakai's wish.

00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:10.654
Please don't try and stop me.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:35.679
<i>This is me. My hair streams across...</i>

00:01:35.888 --> 00:01:40.267
<i>...my cheeks dyed red</i>

00:01:40.476 --> 00:01:44.438
<i>I am me... A grain of determination</i>

00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:49.193
<i>That was how it began</i>

00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:59.828
<i>If there is a tomorrow that is not
hazed over by hope or despair,</i>

00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:01.205
<i>(simple as that)</i>

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:03.707
<i>I will not forget</i>

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:09.255
<i>This pain is the promise we made that day</i>

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:12.258
<i>I want to make it come true, I can't, I will</i>

00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:19.223
<i>At night I grab the void and awaken
to something in the morning</i>

00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:29.191
<i>I merely soar into the endless sky,
taking the shackles called "reason" Yes,</i>

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.153
<i>"That is all.</i> "

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.596
That's...

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:04.935
That's the reason you can't be with me?

00:03:07.521 --> 00:03:09.356
Those feelings...

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:13.736
What we felt back then...

00:03:15.988 --> 00:03:18.699
Why can't you believe them?

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:23.787
<i>Yum...</i>

00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:29.251
You idiot!

00:03:31.503 --> 00:03:34.214
Idiot!

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:40.637
Idiot!

00:03:45.726 --> 00:03:47.853
You lived in the world of humans, Master.

00:03:48.062 --> 00:03:51.815
I'm surprised you don't
know how to handle women better.

00:03:52.858 --> 00:03:55.069
That was never a talent of mine.

00:03:55.277 --> 00:03:58.697
You could give me several
thousands of years' worth of lessons.

00:03:58.906 --> 00:04:01.950
Unfortunately, it's never
been a talent of mine, either.

00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:07.414
We'll attack that!

00:04:07.623 --> 00:04:09.541
U-Understood, indeed.

00:04:12.878 --> 00:04:15.005
Th-They're...

00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:18.258
Throw me!

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:25.974
This is the Grand Order Psalm...

00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:29.728
Yes, and this ring is Corde.

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:33.107
A Treasure that can be loaded with an
Unrestricted Method and fired as a bullet.

00:04:33.315 --> 00:04:34.733
I see.

00:04:34.942 --> 00:04:38.195
I don't know how you got the Psalm,

00:04:38.404 --> 00:04:40.364
but I suppose it would be effective.

00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:42.991
I have more than this!

00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:51.834
Take this.

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:08.517
And I have more than this, as well.

00:05:09.643 --> 00:05:13.605
This is important to me.
I've made it so it can protect itself.

00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:21.447
"What the Wind Calls"

00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:34.001
It doesn't appear to be going well.

00:05:34.209 --> 00:05:37.254
He's pretty strong, too...

00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:38.881
What?

00:05:45.179 --> 00:05:47.931
As usual.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.267
Yeah, I'm sure it's one of Dad's...

00:05:50.476 --> 00:05:52.895
Sale Habichtsburg!

00:05:53.103 --> 00:05:59.610
Today is our special
"payback for all you've done" day!

00:05:59.818 --> 00:06:01.653
Prepare yourself...

00:06:10.871 --> 00:06:14.708
One-hit kill ultimate weapon!

00:06:14.917 --> 00:06:23.842
The miracle of science,
Excellent 252580, the Ultimate Fist Circle!

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.184
I guess this is bad.

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:34.394
Yeah. Probably.

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:45.822
Jeez... They're having
all that fun outside.

00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:48.784
Why do I have to stay hidden?

00:06:48.992 --> 00:06:52.329
They're the decoys, and we're
the ones with the real job to do.

00:06:52.538 --> 00:06:55.123
Can't complain about that.

00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:56.833
Yeah, I suppose.

00:06:57.751 --> 00:07:02.798
If we want to help them,
we have to do our job.

00:07:03.006 --> 00:07:05.634
Yeah, I guess, but...

00:07:05.842 --> 00:07:07.719
Will we really make it in time?

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:13.100
Indeed. I didn't expect
her to be directly above us.

00:07:13.308 --> 00:07:17.729
Yeah, if she's something
they need, they'll protect her well.

00:07:17.938 --> 00:07:19.565
Let's go.

00:07:45.507 --> 00:07:47.759
Where did he come from?

00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:51.638
No... More importantly...

00:07:51.847 --> 00:07:54.850
He's trying to bring down this tower.

00:08:00.939 --> 00:08:04.985
Bel-Peol! Protect yourself!

00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:39.436
I guess it worked.

00:08:44.107 --> 00:08:47.402
Am I going to die?

00:08:48.737 --> 00:08:54.785
No... If it ends here, there wasn't
any point in my coming.

00:08:56.453 --> 00:08:59.915
They didn't want to say goodbye,

00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:02.250
but they did anyway.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:05.045
There was love.

00:09:05.879 --> 00:09:15.472
<i>As the glow of the sunset
sky dyes the city and your profile</i>

00:09:16.014 --> 00:09:22.145
Sometimes it's still love, even when
you do something they don't want...

00:09:22.145 --> 00:09:28.151
<i>what are you thinking,
watching, and feeling?</i>

00:09:28.151 --> 00:09:29.736
Pheles-san is doing something
Johann-san wouldn't want.

00:09:29.736 --> 00:09:37.703
<i>Even if we can't see our
future further down the road,</i>

00:09:37.703 --> 00:09:38.203
Because they're both in love.

00:09:38.203 --> 00:09:43.875
<i>I will hold your hand</i>

00:09:43.875 --> 00:09:44.167
because she didn't
really want me to use it.

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:50.966
<i>And race to the ends of the earth</i>

00:09:50.966 --> 00:09:51.883
<i>'an.</i>

00:09:52.384 --> 00:09:57.848
<i>All the tears,
lies, sadness, and regrets</i>

00:09:57.848 --> 00:09:58.724
Cut this!

00:09:58.724 --> 00:10:04.521
<i>Are proof that I was here with you</i>

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:13.238
<i>I believe "goodbye" is the beginning
of memories only couples can have</i>

00:10:13.447 --> 00:10:16.950
<i>So I swear upon my heart</i>

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.077
I'm going to try it.

00:10:19.077 --> 00:10:25.500
<i>That someday, again...!</i>

00:10:26.084 --> 00:10:29.379
It will put Sakai-kun in danger.

00:10:29.588 --> 00:10:33.884
It may ruin Shana-chan's plan.

00:10:34.092 --> 00:10:38.180
But I think it's for the best.

00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:40.766
For that, I'm willing
to throw away my life.

00:10:40.974 --> 00:10:42.392
No...

00:10:47.439 --> 00:10:49.441
I won't throw it away.

00:10:51.485 --> 00:10:53.570
I'll make it worth something!

00:11:07.626 --> 00:11:09.795
I heard you.

00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:12.380
So very, very strong...

00:11:20.514 --> 00:11:22.516
Pheles-san?

00:11:22.724 --> 00:11:28.396
The Giralda is a Treasure created to
allow humans to use Unrestricted Methods.

00:11:35.195 --> 00:11:42.327
Humans cannot concentrate
strongly enough on a single thought.

00:11:42.536 --> 00:11:46.039
So it lets them invoke
an Unrestricted Method

00:11:46.248 --> 00:11:50.168
by using their resolve
to sacrifice themselves.

00:11:50.377 --> 00:11:52.003
Then I...

00:11:52.212 --> 00:11:53.463
You will not die.

00:11:53.672 --> 00:11:56.591
Did you give me
this because you knew?

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:57.592
The opposite.

00:11:57.801 --> 00:12:01.888
I gave it to you because I thought
you would never, ever use it.

00:12:03.431 --> 00:12:08.144
But you made this miracle happen,
and brought me here.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:10.480
I, who can change everything,

00:12:10.689 --> 00:12:14.025
in the place where
everything is decided...

00:12:21.741 --> 00:12:23.577
Kazumi Yoshida.

00:12:24.202 --> 00:12:29.040
I shall go, in answer to your miracle,
and grant your wish.

00:12:34.462 --> 00:12:35.881
Pheles...

00:12:39.426 --> 00:12:41.803
I shall change what is here,

00:12:42.012 --> 00:12:46.808
and I shall fulfill my
unwanted promise with Johann.

00:12:54.107 --> 00:12:55.358
Pheles...

00:12:55.567 --> 00:12:57.861
Why didn't you tell me anything?

00:13:01.406 --> 00:13:02.782
Pheles!

00:13:02.991 --> 00:13:04.492
I'm sorry.

00:13:07.537 --> 00:13:09.039
Pheles!

00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:16.963
To have her summoned here,
at this late hour...

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:23.428
I have you.

00:13:31.019 --> 00:13:33.021
Wake up, Johann.

00:13:37.776 --> 00:13:39.194
Yo.

00:13:39.444 --> 00:13:41.363
Hello there, I suppose.

00:13:41.571 --> 00:13:44.950
Yuji Sakai-kun and Snake of the Festival.

00:13:45.158 --> 00:13:46.952
I'm taking it back.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:52.040
Our Treasure, the Midnight Lost Child.

00:13:52.248 --> 00:13:53.166
Yuji!

00:13:53.375 --> 00:13:55.001
I won't let you!

00:14:00.674 --> 00:14:03.176
If you were inside me,

00:14:03.385 --> 00:14:07.889
then you should know
what Yuji Sakai was planning.

00:14:08.098 --> 00:14:10.016
Both of them, I suppose.

00:14:10.225 --> 00:14:13.395
I can understand
his passion and devotion,

00:14:13.603 --> 00:14:14.938
but I can't agree with it.

00:14:15.146 --> 00:14:15.855
What?

00:14:16.064 --> 00:14:19.484
I don't mind the means,
but I don't like the ends.

00:14:19.693 --> 00:14:20.318
The ends?

00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:25.907
Yes. The ends for
Yuji Sakai-kun, who isn't a God.

00:14:26.783 --> 00:14:30.996
It's a noble vow,
but it's boring and not any fun.

00:14:31.204 --> 00:14:33.540
And more than anything,
everyone ends up unhappy.

00:14:33.748 --> 00:14:35.500
I can't cooperate with that.

00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:37.335
This isn't a game!

00:14:37.544 --> 00:14:42.632
Yuji Sakai-kun, you're trying
to make the ending too clean.

00:14:43.675 --> 00:14:46.302
"I did this, so I have to do that," you say.

00:14:46.511 --> 00:14:48.638
And that forces you into this.

00:14:48.847 --> 00:14:52.267
I'll do everything I can,
and then take the punishment for it.

00:14:52.475 --> 00:14:54.436
What's wrong with that?!

00:14:54.644 --> 00:14:58.064
Isn't it wrong to make
the girl you like unhappy?

00:14:59.357 --> 00:15:01.026
If love is behind your whole plan,

00:15:01.234 --> 00:15:04.821
then I think it's okay
to act a bit more selfishly...

00:15:06.114 --> 00:15:08.616
Shana would never allow that.

00:15:08.825 --> 00:15:10.827
You haven't even
told her the whole thing.

00:15:11.036 --> 00:15:12.662
So how do you know?

00:15:12.871 --> 00:15:15.623
You've been so obsessed with
the pursuit of your goal...

00:15:15.832 --> 00:15:19.461
I also think not paying
more attention to her is a mistake.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.631
You don't think
Shana would understand?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.509
I'm not optimistic enough to expect that!

00:15:26.718 --> 00:15:30.722
Revealing the plan could
endanger the creation of Xanadu!

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.891
So, your hopes are dangerous...

00:15:33.099 --> 00:15:36.644
You really are stubborn. Or rather...

00:15:36.853 --> 00:15:40.607
I see... I understand now.

00:15:42.776 --> 00:15:46.237
You're underestimating love!

00:15:46.446 --> 00:15:48.239
What?

00:15:48.448 --> 00:15:50.450
You tell yourself you
can't show them your love.

00:15:50.658 --> 00:15:52.786
You won't use it as an excuse.

00:15:52.994 --> 00:15:55.622
You keep making your world smaller.

00:15:57.373 --> 00:16:00.877
Love can push aside logic and self-interest,
and accomplish anything.

00:16:01.086 --> 00:16:03.463
It's pretty amazing.

00:16:03.671 --> 00:16:06.508
You expect me to believe that,
just because you said it?

00:16:06.716 --> 00:16:08.760
I thought you'd say that.

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:12.472
You've decided that you
can't be allowed to have happiness,

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:16.601
so you've thrust aside what
you have now, and come this far.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:19.229
You have no right to say that to me!

00:16:19.437 --> 00:16:21.648
What I think about it is up to me.

00:16:21.856 --> 00:16:23.983
It's all right, Johann.

00:16:24.192 --> 00:16:25.819
So is doing this.

00:16:32.033 --> 00:16:34.744
It's fine. I'll give it back to you.

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:36.329
What are you going to do?

00:16:36.538 --> 00:16:40.083
I'm going to change your situation!

00:16:40.291 --> 00:16:42.043
Come here, Pheles.

00:16:42.252 --> 00:16:43.878
Johann!

00:16:47.549 --> 00:16:50.135
I did everything.

00:16:50.343 --> 00:16:52.137
I didn't want to, but I did it anyway.

00:16:52.345 --> 00:16:54.347
I tried really, really hard.

00:16:54.556 --> 00:16:56.224
Thank you, Pheles.

00:16:56.432 --> 00:16:58.393
I'm sorry to make you
do something so painful.

00:16:58.601 --> 00:17:02.147
My beloved Pheles, no one will ever...

00:17:02.355 --> 00:17:03.898
Yes, Johann.

00:17:04.107 --> 00:17:06.943
Tear us apart again...

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.381
Get in!

00:17:32.927 --> 00:17:34.345
Bye!

00:17:36.431 --> 00:17:37.849
Damn!

00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:39.225
Floor it!

00:17:39.434 --> 00:17:40.852
Right!

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.109
Go with them for now, Kazumi.

00:17:49.277 --> 00:17:51.613
The one that went up was an illusion.

00:17:51.821 --> 00:17:54.532
The real bus was heading toward the surface.

00:17:54.741 --> 00:17:55.366
In other words...

00:17:55.575 --> 00:17:58.161
What a bunch of jerks...

00:17:58.369 --> 00:17:59.787
Yuji!

00:18:00.038 --> 00:18:03.666
You lost your detection ability, didn't you?

00:18:03.875 --> 00:18:05.877
An effect of Johann's leaving?

00:18:06.085 --> 00:18:07.212
I don't know.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:11.674
But now I have better things
to do than to find out why.

00:18:32.195 --> 00:18:33.613
What?

00:18:35.698 --> 00:18:38.910
That isn't a nice way to greet a guest.

00:18:39.118 --> 00:18:42.038
Yeah. I'm sorry to
force myself on you like this,

00:18:42.247 --> 00:18:44.374
but do you need an
escort for your escape?

00:18:44.582 --> 00:18:49.462
If they have your strength, sure.

00:18:51.839 --> 00:18:54.968
I didn't expect Hyakki Yakou to show up.

00:18:55.176 --> 00:18:58.972
So the Tuner infiltrated,
to get them inside.

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.849
But what's the point of taking her?

00:19:02.058 --> 00:19:05.603
Who knows? They've caused
a good deal of damage.

00:19:05.812 --> 00:19:09.565
But in the end,
we'll make it all work out.

00:19:11.109 --> 00:19:12.568
Professor.

00:19:12.777 --> 00:19:14.862
Is the tower's tuning not finished yet?

00:19:15.071 --> 00:19:16.781
Yes, General!

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:21.286
We've just finished the density
calculations and VR simulations...

00:19:21.494 --> 00:19:23.288
Domino!

00:19:23.496 --> 00:19:30.503
Domino, are you trying to
ruin my beautiful climactic scene?

00:19:30.712 --> 00:19:33.715
I'm very sorry, Professor!

00:19:33.923 --> 00:19:35.633
So when will it be done?

00:19:35.842 --> 00:19:36.968
When?

00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:38.636
We can do it whenever...

00:19:38.845 --> 00:19:42.348
We can do it right now, in fact!

00:20:17.508 --> 00:20:22.263
P-Professor! The machinery
control system is exposed!

00:20:22.472 --> 00:20:24.724
Didn't you remove the monster
form control room functions

00:20:24.932 --> 00:20:26.601
when the Strategist got mad at you?

00:20:26.809 --> 00:20:27.894
Domino!

00:20:28.102 --> 00:20:34.192
Call it a self-sacrifice,
to benefit the tower's strength!

00:20:40.156 --> 00:20:42.909
Don't make me worry
about things I haven't planned for,

00:20:43.117 --> 00:20:44.660
Professor Dantalion.

00:20:44.869 --> 00:20:46.704
We're saved...

00:20:46.913 --> 00:20:49.332
Can you send it back inside?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.542
I'm prepared for anything.

00:20:51.751 --> 00:20:54.045
Close canopy!

00:20:57.757 --> 00:20:59.175
Jeez“.

00:21:02.011 --> 00:21:04.680
This wasn't part of the plan,
but we managed to pull it off somehow.

00:21:04.889 --> 00:21:08.684
It might be easier than
just blowing up the whole thing.

00:21:08.893 --> 00:21:11.521
But we'll be destroying
it all, either way.

00:21:11.729 --> 00:21:15.233
Then let's perform the
important task they assigned us.

00:21:15.441 --> 00:21:19.654
Let's do it, and make sure
we don't collapse under the pressure.

00:21:25.493 --> 00:21:28.830
Why do they keep
fighting without advancing?

00:21:29.038 --> 00:21:31.999
We're simply waiting
for Xanadu's creation.

00:21:32.208 --> 00:21:35.628
Time is on our side.

00:21:35.837 --> 00:21:39.215
This is strange.
I don't understand their plan.

00:21:39.215 --> 00:21:42.176
<i>The moon and stars
are illuminating me</i>

00:21:42.385 --> 00:21:45.805
<i>On top of the carpet with
dancing sparks</i>

00:21:46.013 --> 00:21:49.475
<i>You are right in front of me,
glowing red in the light</i>

00:21:49.684 --> 00:21:53.104
<i>Your honest eyes are twinkling</i>

00:21:53.312 --> 00:21:56.691
<i>The two footsteps, they head
toward the distant yonder</i>

00:21:56.899 --> 00:22:01.571
<i>The words I told you said,
"Let's leave everything behind"</i>

00:22:01.779 --> 00:22:07.034
<i>Fly toward the future</i>

00:22:07.243 --> 00:22:11.539
<i>The motive has a strong grasp on
my heart Yes, this is the ultimate descent</i>

00:22:11.747 --> 00:22:15.168
<i>The two of us are fellow soldiers
flattering one another's pulses</i>

00:22:15.376 --> 00:22:18.588
<i>If you are going to protect your love,
you cannot reject battle</i>

00:22:18.796 --> 00:22:22.133
<i>Without fudging a phrase,
we rhyme down this hot path</i>

00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:25.636
<i>Passing each other by, quarreling</i>

00:22:25.845 --> 00:22:29.307
<i>Set free from the enchantment</i>

00:22:29.515 --> 00:22:32.852
<i>If you are going to leave on a journey,</i>

00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:36.606
<i>I will never let go of your hand again</i>

00:22:36.814 --> 00:22:40.109
<i>Do you still remember the first time</i>

00:22:40.318 --> 00:22:43.821
<i>Our eyes locked,
just as it happened?</i>

00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:47.158
<i>Even if I am engulfed
by the vortex of slumber,</i>

00:22:47.366 --> 00:22:53.039
<i>It will not vanish,
I won't let it--It's our dream</i>

00:22:53.247 --> 00:22:54.457
<i>To be as ONE</i>

00:22:54.665 --> 00:22:59.295
<i>When you placed your hands
on your cheeks and laughed</i>

00:22:59.504 --> 00:23:01.756
<i>I thought, "I want to protect you"</i>

00:23:01.964 --> 00:23:05.718
<i>We took a roundabout path, huh?
But I've realized</i>

00:23:05.927 --> 00:23:09.347
<i>That I live just for you</i>

00:23:09.555 --> 00:23:12.934
<i>Snow of light flutters down the sky</i>

00:23:13.142 --> 00:23:16.521
<i>Where the waning moon
and stars go to snuggle</i>

00:23:16.729 --> 00:23:20.024
<i>The story we have written</i>

00:23:20.233 --> 00:23:24.362
<i>Will continue on forever</i>

00:23:25.905 --> 00:23:28.491
The battle over the creation
of Xanadu grows fiercer,

00:23:28.699 --> 00:23:31.369
and everyone puts their
lives on the line for their beliefs.

00:23:31.577 --> 00:23:34.288
Meanwhile, Rofocale,
whom Frieder has captured,

00:23:34.497 --> 00:23:35.957
receives an unexpected request.

00:23:36.165 --> 00:23:38.042
Next time,
on Shakugan no Shana Final:

00:23:38.251 --> 00:23:39.752
"The Egg of the World."
